================================================================================
CHANGE 8 — exits run to completion
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
closeDocked: travel = effectsCon.offsetWidth, curve "cubic-bezier(.7,0,.84,0)"
drop close:  curve "cubic-bezier(.7,0,.84,0)"

NEW_SECTION
var EXIT_CURVE = "cubic-bezier(.4,0,1,1)";
closeDocked: travel = Math.ceil(effectsCon.offsetWidth * 1.25), curve EXIT_CURVE
drop close:  curve EXIT_CURVE

REASON
Reported: slideLeft was not visibly exiting back out the way it came. Frame sampling showed the steep ease-in left the panel nearly still (48px in 267ms) and the core slide's timed callback removed it at 400ms while it was still about half on screen, so it vanished instead of sliding out. A steady accelerate curve plus a target a quarter past the edge now takes it fully off screen before removal: slideLeft by ~340ms (moving right), slideRight by ~345ms (moving left), drop by ~260ms (moving up).

================================================================================
CHANGE 9 — sideways exits continue through the far edge
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
    var travel = Math.ceil(layer.effectsCon.offsetWidth * 1.25);
    var direction = layer.dock == "right" ? "toRight" : "toLeft"; //back out the way it came
    $$.sm(slider).slide[direction](dockConfigs(layer, [0, -travel], 400, EXIT_CURVE), ...

NEW_SECTION
    layer.effectsCon.style["overflow"] = "visible";
    var travel = Math.ceil(window.innerWidth * 1.25);
    var direction = layer.dock == "right" ? "toLeft" : "toRight"; //the way it was already moving
    $$.sm(slider).slide[direction](dockConfigs(layer, [0, travel], 500, EXIT_CURVE), ...

REASON
Clarified requirement: slideLeft must leave by continuing left (across the screen and out of the left edge), not by reversing back to the right; slideRight mirrors it. The container stops clipping on close so the panel can cross the viewport; the overlay already hides horizontal overflow. Travel is the viewport width (plus the 25% timer margin) measured from the docked edge, over 500ms. Verified: slideLeft right edge past x=0 and slideRight left edge past x=1200 by ~450ms, no horizontal page scroll.

================================================================================
CHANGE 10 — exits reverse again; both sides move by "left"
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
closeDocked: effectsCon overflow visible; travel = innerWidth * 1.25; direction = same as entry; [0, travel]
dockConfigs(layer, x, ...) -> positionProperty: layer.dock   ("right" for slideLeft)

NEW_SECTION
closeDocked: clipping kept; travel = panel width * 1.25; direction = back out the way it came;
             [0, offEdge(layer, travel)], 400ms, EXIT_CURVE
openDocked:  [offEdge(layer, travel), 0]
dockConfigs(x, ...) -> positionProperty: "left" always
function offEdge(layer, travel) { return layer.dock == "right" ? travel : -travel; }

REASON
The user reported no animation and that slideRight left to the right. The intended behaviour is the panel leaving back through its own edge (slideLeft exits right, slideRight exits left), so CHANGE 9 is reverted. The missing animation: slideLeft moved the panel with "right", and only the uncommitted core.css lists "right" in .vSlide.pos's transition; the committed core.css (or a cached copy) lists only left and top, so the panel jumped. Both sides now move by "left" (offset +width for the right dock, -width for the left), which every core.css version transitions. Verified in headless Chromium against both the working-tree and the committed core.css: slideLeft in 1200->700, out 700->1325; slideRight in -500->0, out 0->-583; no errors.

